# Copy to .env.local and fill in privately. Never commit .env.local.
# Names only here; `tools/demo.sh --check` tells you what is missing (it never prints values).
# Step-by-step: docs/run-on-your-chert-line.md

# ---- LiveKit Cloud project (Settings > API keys). All three from the same project.
LIVEKIT_URL=wss://YOUR_PROJECT.livekit.cloud
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=YOUR_LIVEKIT_API_KEY
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=YOUR_LIVEKIT_API_SECRET

# The name this agent registers with LiveKit; chert dev and chert doctor read it too.
# Pick something unique to you, e.g. onset-<your initials>.
AGENT_NAME=onset-YOUR_SUFFIX

# ---- Voice. The first key present is the main voice; the others are fallbacks.
# ElevenLabs is also needed for the sentence check (Scribe speech-to-text).
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVEN_VOICE_ID=EXAVITQu4vr4xnSDxMaL   # Sarah (default); River SAz9YHcvj6GT2YYXdXww; Brian nPczCjzI2devNBz1zQrb
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---- Chert project API (caregiver iMessage with the join link, line health).
# Create a project API key (starts with ftk_) at https://app.trychert.com/developer
CHERT_API_KEY=
CHERT_PROJECT_ID=
# Optional: the line to use (else the project's first line).
# CHERT_LINE_ID=
# Optional: pin a different Chert CLI version for tools/chert.sh.
# CHERT_CLI_VERSION=0.1.0-beta.20

# ---- Patients. Profiles map a caller's phone to their baseline and caregiver:
# copy config/patients.example.json to config/patients.json (gitignored) and edit it.
# ONSET_PATIENTS_FILE=config/patients.json
# Without a profiles file, one person is configured here:
# ONSET_PATIENT_ID=demo
# ONSET_PATIENT_NAME=
# ONSET_CAREGIVER_NAME=
# ONSET_CAREGIVER_PHONE=

# ---- Escalation: on ESCALATE / UNCLEAR the caregiver is brought into the live call.
# link  iMessage the caregiver a summary and a private link that opens this call in their
#       browser: they see the caller and Onset's screen, and (with talk on) the caller hears
#       and sees them through Onset (Chert allows only one audio publisher per call). Default.
# off   summary iMessage only.
# ONSET_CAREGIVER_JOIN=link
# ONSET_CAREGIVER_TALK=1
# The caregiver page: web/caregiver/index.html hosted anywhere static (e.g. GitHub Pages);
# tokens travel in the #fragment, never to that server. Unset: LiveKit Meet, watch-only.
# ONSET_CAREGIVER_PAGE=https://<you>.github.io/onset/caregiver/
# How long the caregiver's link works, in seconds.
# ONSET_CAREGIVER_LINK_TTL_S=900

# ---- SAFETY GATE. Real iMessages and calls happen ONLY with this set to 1.
# Anything else is a dry run: logged and shown on the dashboard, nothing is sent.
ONSET_LIVE_ACTIONS=0
# Keep some kinds dry even when live, comma list of: imessage, invite, call
# ONSET_LIVE_ACTIONS_DENY=

# ---- Sentence step: stop recording when the caller stops talking (1) or always use the timer (0).
# ONSET_SPEECH_VAD=1

# The video Onset sends back. Upright 540x960 by default: a Chert line whose video_framing is
# "fill" crops a wide picture to its middle third and cuts the captions off (docs/video-framing.md).
# ONSET_FRAME=portrait turns whatever size you give upright; ONSET_FRAME=landscape keeps it wide.
# Bigger is sharper and slower: 720x1280 is the most worth trying.
# ONSET_FRAME=portrait
# OUT_WIDTH=540
# OUT_HEIGHT=960

# After a check-in finds a change, FaceTime the caregiver too, once the person's call has ended,
# and tell them what Onset found (docs/escalation.md). off (default) | after. Needs CHERT_API_KEY,
# CHERT_PROJECT_ID, a caregiver phone that has joined the line, and ONSET_LIVE_ACTIONS=1 to be real.
# ONSET_CAREGIVER_CALL=off

# The agent's worker (onset/worker.py). The defaults suit one line on a laptop, in `start` and `dev`:
# one process kept ready, never refuses a call for CPU load, any free health port.
# ONSET_IDLE_PROCESSES=1
# ONSET_LOAD_THRESHOLD=inf
# ONSET_HEALTH_PORT=0

# Record calls to recordings/ (contains a face and voice; keep private).
# ONSET_RECORD=0

# Voice order, best first (default elevenlabs,gemini,openai). Put gemini first if ElevenLabs runs out of credits.
# ONSET_VOICE_ORDER=gemini,elevenlabs,openai
